EVT3026 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat7 [H] - I'm sorry, but I cant promise you something that may very well be impossible. It really doesn't matter how well our plan may be going if it only takes one mistake for all of this to come crashing down on us. Just remember that I am doing everything in my power to see this through.
EVT3027 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat6 [B] - Desperate? Markus, we have completely run out of options, we really have no other choice. Can you at least give me something to work with here?
EVT3028 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat5 [H] - Do you really think this operation stands a chance? I'm starting to fear we're becoming too desperate.
EVT3029 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat1 [H] - Think I would go so far as to say that they might even be the best ones for this job all things considered.
EVT3030 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat4 [H] - Its still impossible to say, there's just too many variables to consider. Sure we've hit all of our energy quotas thus far, but the core is starting to destabilize with every activation. At our current rate, this installation might just fall apart long before we have enough power, but I simply do not know.
EVT3031 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat2 [H] - I mean, what they've been able to accomplish on such short notice is remarkable to say the least. Even our old crew would struggle with these quotas.
EVT3032 TEXT x.ChatFrame.Chat3 [B] - Does this mean we'll have enough power?
